WEBVTT

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.270
Last night, someone sent
me the access password.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.730
When I used that to access
Headquarters' computer....

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.130
They're secret files, about us.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.630
What's this?!

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.010
The brutal... and comical truth.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.990
Lost

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.120
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.040
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.960
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.300
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.010
Found

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.260
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.720
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.560
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.650
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.980
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.900
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.610
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.950
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.160
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.530
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:45.000
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.710
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.540
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.420
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.550
It's now or never

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.630
That is what they say

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.720
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.390
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.550
That is what they say

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.720
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.230
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.440
That is what they say

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.850
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.990
The Sad Clown

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.110
Kaito!

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.320
You solved it?
The Puzzle of Fools?

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.800
Erena, tell me about a
harder Puzzle of Fools.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.530
This one's got nothin' to it at all!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.300
W-Well, fine.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.780
Ain't you goin' at kinda a high pace?

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.100
Pushin' too hard could cost you your life.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.410
I can't go takin' things slow.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.540
Freecell's made his
Replica Ring a real one!

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:13.080
If I wanna play a game with
him, I've gotta get stronger.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.900
Kaito...

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.890
I don't like this data.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.700
Each time he solves a Puzzle of Fools,

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.210
the pattern matches when he
almost became a Phi-Brain.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.830
Kaito... Just where
are you trying to go?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.610
What was that?

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.860
Are you serious, Doubt?!

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.070
Yeah.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.370
I will challenge Kaito
Daimon to the final game.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.780
But why now?

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.370
This whole time, we've been
treated like playthings!

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.990
We've been made to believe lies.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.670
If it is Klondike's will...

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.800
Mizerka, what will you do?

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.860
I...

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.360
Melancholy. You're back?

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.040
I was so worried.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:27.720
Mizerka!

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.330
Wait. I want to try
talking to Melancholy.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.210
I won't mention anything
about the Rings.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.070
Melan... choly?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.930
Oh, dear. Sister, you're SO interesting.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.620
Wh-What's so funny, Melancholy?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.820
Say, Sister,

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:01.920
your friend Eve was a
test subject, wasn't she?

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.570
How do you know that?

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.420
She didn't know her Ring was a replica,

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.250
but she was used, and

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.440
tossed away when no longer useful.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.750
Poor girl.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.370
I'm not going.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.370
Don't think I'm like YOU, Sister.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.790
What's with that tone?

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.000
Look, just come with us!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.670
Do you hear me, Melancholy?

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.260
Who do you think you are?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.150
You're just a test subject!

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.740
You really flaunt it, don't you?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.200
Your role as big sister.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.910
I've never once thought you my sister.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.630
It was a game.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.190
You're such a meddlesome busybody

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:50.240
that I played your little game, that's all.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.990
M-Melancholy...

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:57.000
Goodbye, O "Sister" of the Replica Ring.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:19.550
Where's Melancholy?

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:26.040
I... I just want someone to need me.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.500
"Come with me."

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.530
If someone told me that, I'd go.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:35.800
Let's go.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.620
Yes.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.540
It seems your talk has concluded.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.630
Whist!

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.910
Where have you been all this time?

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.160
Even knowing the truth,

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.470
your resolve to offer yourselves
up to the Orpheus Order

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.200
has made Mr. Klondike
tremendously happy.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.560
Mr. Doubt. If you so wish,

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.010
I could provide you with an upgraded Ring.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.480
What was that?!

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.000
Enormous power.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.420
As Mr. Freecell and Mr.
Pinochle were given.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.340
Oh, my. This is...

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.750
What an unusual guest.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.350
I think this is strange.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:49.530
Solving Puzzles of Fools
for Freecell's sake...

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.020
I told you, didn't I?

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.450
Freecell has come close
to being a Phi-Brain.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.150
This is so I can battle him.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.140
So you'll become a Phi-Brain, too?

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.160
The very Phi-Brain that you rejected?

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.610
No! That ain't it.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.170
But I, Ana, think...

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:11.670
Puzzles of Fools are puzzles
for training Phi-Brains.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.450
It turns people to Phi-Brains.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.300
Yeah, but still...

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.770
Anyway, I gotta get stronger.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.690
Then WE shall be your opponents.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.150
The Orpheus Order!

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.900
Doubt! The hell are you doin' here?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.400
Kaito Daimon.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.400
Fight us.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.740
What'd you say?

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:40.830
Cut the crap!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.140
If you all lost,

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.360
weren't you supposed to
never bother us again?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.710
Now you're breakin'
your promise, bastard?!

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:48.870
I'm sorry.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:53.420
Such action runs counter to chivalry,
and I am ashamed.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:01.350
Kaito!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.650
Their Rings aren't real.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.710
They're replicas!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.350
That's right.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:11.900
Our Orpheus Rings are replicas
for the sake of gathering data.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.430
We were never Phi-Brain children...

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.250
Merely test subjects.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.940
We learned this yesterday,
having seen some

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.530
secret Orpheus Order files.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.940
To you, we must look like
sad, pathetic clowns.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.040
However, my loyalty is unwavering.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.260
If I may be the foundation of
Lord Klondike's grand scheme,

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.020
then I gladly offer myself up.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.740
Dude, why?

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.650
Klondike deceived you. So, why?!

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.380
Sure enough, they've both been
swallowed up by the Rings.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.630
What's this?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.110
There's a disturbance
in Mizerka's thoughts.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:01.830
What is this noise?

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.810
After we've collected a
certain percentage of data,

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.540
the Replica Rings will be
completed to make Final Rings.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.010
We will collect our
data for that purpose

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.840
and present it to Lord Klondike.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.530
And my opponent to that end is YOU.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.890
Fight, Kaito Daimon!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.560
Fight us in a game for your life!

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.500
Gimme a break!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.550
Why would I do a game like that?

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.600
Or fight you guys NOW?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.280
Why not do the courtesy of accepting?

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.140
They've swallowed their pride
and confessed everything.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:41.470
Gammon, please make the puzzle.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:42.120
Old dude!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.150
I'd planned on it
without you tellin' me.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:47.830
I'll make a puzzle that'll be their graves!

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.310
Gammon!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.480
Antoinette, help me.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.270
F-Fine.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.090
Hey! What the heck?

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.590
We will borrow POG Japan's premises.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.590
The puzzle shall be there.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.270
My thanks.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.590
Come on, you guys!

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.970
Are all you guys idiots?!

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.200
May I help you?

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:26.450
Eve... My sister. She needs you.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:31.450
No. I am no longer needed.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:37.440
I will not lose.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.210
Kaito... Ana...

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.040
A good puzzle.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:06.440
Truly the work of the man
I acknowledged, Gammon Sakanoue.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.170
This'll be a coffin for you pricks.

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:13.220
This whole steel frame will fall and you'll croak.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.840
Will you not fight?

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.090
Nah. I don't wanna die.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.410
Kaito. Ana. Crush 'em with
everything you've got!

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.350
Otherwise, you guys'll die!

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.970
I know.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.810
Sure thing!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.010
Can I save them?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.230
They've been swallowed by the

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.730
Rings, are still loyal
to the Orpheus Order...

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.570
Let's do this thing!

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:44.190
Puzzle time... let's begin!

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:46.530
Here we go!

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.750
Here I, Ana, go!

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.610
Sure enough, this is a fearsome puzzle.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.850
Players can only move
along one steel bar.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:32.620
However, they can't move to
a bar another player is on.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:36.270
They can stay on a bar
for just one turn.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.800
Staying for two turns isn't allowed.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.310
Players can drop three bars at a time.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:45.180
They can drop only a full line of bars.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.610
They can't drop a row of
bars another player is on.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:51.410
Of course, bars that separate from

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.600
the puzzle frame will collapse and fall.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:58.830
Also, whoever manages to drop
even one other player wins.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.750
So fast! There's no hesitation!

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:17.820
Those guys are good.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.190
It's the power of their Rings.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.130
That's not all.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.460
They don't fear death,

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.510
and have a sense of loyalty and purpose.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:31.210
Ana, I'm countin' on ya!

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:33.010
Certainly!

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.060
Hmm, that one?

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.810
Maybe that one. Or this one.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.500
That one!

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:42.880
Just fooling.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.530
Sure enough, it's THIS one!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.530
A meaningless play.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.240
As always, a disagreeable person.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.410
Disagreeable...

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:56.570
Stop. That's enough.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.370
Enough.

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.170
Eve... Forgave that person.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:09.620
Why... do I hate him?

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.090
Now he's got no choice!

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.570
A good play, Mizerka.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:29.550
Huh?

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.490
I stay. However...

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.370
Why do you hesitate, Kaito Daimon?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.900
Throw everything at us and crush us.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:45.380
Otherwise, we shall crush you!

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.130
You don't gotta tell me!

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.200
Kaito... He's not serious, is he?

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:55.120
He cannot help them unless
he fights seriously.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.970
Can I really save them?

00:15:58.970 --> 00:15:59.880
Me?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.040
Kaito!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.150
I, Ana, think...

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.440
You shouldn't think at all!

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:14.660
Don't think, just enjoy the
puzzle for all it's worth.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:16.670
Ana...

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:19.420
You're right.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.960
If I've gotta do it,
I might as well enjoy it.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:23.560
This puzzle!

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.710
I'm stayin', too. Also...

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:31.380
What?!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.080
For him to notice the
trap Mizerka set...

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:37.810
Well done, Kaito Daimon. However...

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.310
Not yet!

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:40.810
Jumpy-jump!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.060
Our advantage is unwavering.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.810
Yeah, right!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.060
I won't let you!

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.920
Leapy-leap!

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:49.570
What?!

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.180
Good one, Ana.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:54.550
Yay!

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.030
They've turned the tables.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:57.990
Yes.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:00.020
Kaito!

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.910
If I'd dropped the bar that he's on,

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.990
Kaito Daimon would have fallen.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:11.170
He saw that completely,
and prevented me from doing so.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:15.680
Not just Kaito Daimon,
but Ana Gram as well.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.760
Incredible. Are these
true Phi-Brain children?

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.680
You look like you're having fun, Doubt.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.110
"Fun"?

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.760
Indeed. Puzzles are fun.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.670
Mizerka, you look like
you're having fun, too.

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:37.840
Because you told me to come, Doubt.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:42.710
Since I was little, no
one has ever needed me.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:46.250
I hated myself for that,

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.920
and lived my life
thinking I had to change.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.940
I was happy.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:53.970
I see.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.160
Kaito Daimon!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.140
This clinches it!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:10.900
I stay.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:15.300
Yahoo!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.390
I stay.

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:22.850
I stay, too.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.090
With Kaito's next move, it's all over.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:43.970
So it's come to this, eh?

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.820
Excellently done, Kaito Daimon.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:53.210
I have no shame losing
to one such as you.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.630
Now then. Finish this.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:01.970
Hurry! Finish it!

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.240
I say no!

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.950
No. I don't want to die.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:10.620
I want to keep solving puzzles!

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:11.920
Mizerka!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.760
So do you, Doubt!

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.670
Isn't that right?
I won't let you say I'm wrong!

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.070
That smiling face, looking so happy

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.870
as you're solving puzzles...

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:24.180
That's the true you!

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:27.540
Why?

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:32.440
Why can't you be as you are?!

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.100
Mizerka!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:54.070
That's the mercy of a
knight... No, a warrior.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:58.150
The system in this area
completely blocks radio waves.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.670
The data they collected
wasn't able to be sent.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.410
Indeed.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:06.720
You all! You should've said something!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.780
Are you okay? Hang in there.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:32.830
Doubt. This is the first time
I've seen you smile solving a puzzle.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:34.950
P-Pinochle?

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.340
You're alive?

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.320
It was a good smile.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.970
Sure enough,
you've always liked puzzles.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:48.020
I was the one who sent
Mizerka the password.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:51.270
I'm glad. They helped you guys.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.770
D-Doubt...

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:01.870
Gammon Sakanoue.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.910
I still feel no shame.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.910
That I used your sister.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.020
Gammon!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.050
Bastard!

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:16.630
I'm sorry.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:24.780
Dude...

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:32.280
I, Ana, think Mizerka wanted this.

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:36.980
To say bye-bye to the
Ring, and to be saved.

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:38.800
I think so, too.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:43.190
The disturbance in her
thoughts reflected that emotion.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:46.800
Eve will probably be happy.

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:14.600
Melancholy. I envy you.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:18.060
For that Ring you possess...

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:25.490
So you've come. Just as I calculated.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.230 --> 00:24:04.010
Klondike of the Orpheus Order...

00:24:04.770 --> 00:24:07.300
decides to rely on a
"Suzuki" from Nagano.

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.960
To improve his puzzle aptitude,

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:13.010
he memorizes all of the school's textbooks.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.810
You're amazing, Suzuki!

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:15.850
Thank you.

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:19.270
So, you didn't simply
study the normal way?

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:20.370
Next time,

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.080
"The Ruler Atop the Board"

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:26.670
The Ruler Atop the Board

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.230
I shall be counting on you.
